y be included or not, but if a node's local counter includes an add it never acked (e.g., it counted locally but then crashed/was blocked), that's fine (it's in the acceptable set as long as it's in the range).\n\nWait careful: the acceptable set is the sum of definite adds plus any subset of info adds. If our final value includes an info add that we included, fine. If we include an info add twice, bad. If we include part of an add (impossible with ints)... fine.\n\nBut: if a node processes an add, includes it locally, and then the client times out and retries? Maelstrom client doesn't retry; each op is a single request. So there's no duplicate-request risk... Actually, Maelstrom's client may resend on timeout? Let's check maelstrom/client.clj. I believe no retry: `c/rpc!` sends once and waits with a timeout; on timeout, throws, and the op is marked :info. Let's check.\n\nImportant detail: does the client retry? If it retries the same msg_id, and we add twice, that would exceed. Let's check client.clj.\n\nAlso I need to check how the nemesis/partition healing interacts with final reads, to determine timing.\n\nLet me look at client.clj and core.clj (final generator + nemesis stop ordering).", "text": "", "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {"command": "cd /tmp && python3 -c \"\nimport zipfile\nz=zipfile.ZipFile('/opt/maelstrom/lib/maelstrom.jar')\nprint(z.read('maelstrom/client.clj').decode())\n\""}, "arguments_error": null, "id": "call_01a204402013731387cc80c3", "name": "shell"}], "usage": {"input_tokens": 27631, "output_tokens": 820}}}
